# veo-audit cron schedule, read by supercronic in the `scheduler` container.
# Times are in America/Denver (set via TZ env on the scheduler container) so
# the daily SLA window correctly tracks DST. The 2-min ingest cadence drifts
# by 60 minutes twice a year at DST transitions — acceptable for a compliance
# audit; missed cycles are caught by the staleness check on the next firing.

# Ingest: every 2 minutes (cadence cutover 2026-07-07; was */10 since v3.0).
# The upstream feed is generated per-request (last_updated stamps at fetch
# time, ttl=0), so any cadence returns current fleet state; 2 min tightens
# trip-duration resolution to ±2 min for the burn-rate work. NOTE: the live
# schedule is the admin-editable copy on the scheduler_state volume
# (/app/state/crontab) — this file only seeds fresh environments. Changing
# cadence in prod = edit /admin/scheduler/edit to match.
*/2 * * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli ingest_cycle

# Daily SLA window: 9:00 AM Denver, DST-aware. Computes the 6-9 AM window
# that just closed. Idempotent via ON CONFLICT.
0 9 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli daily_sla

# Daily trip/popularity rollup: same 9:00 AM slot, but rolls up
# YESTERDAY's full calendar day (today isn't over yet). Separate command
# from daily_sla so a failure in one doesn't block or mask the other.
0 9 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli daily_trips

# Archive: fires daily at 02:00 AM Denver but only acts if >= archive_hours
# (config.json; 24 since the 2-min cadence cutover — a 48h window at 2-min
# is ~12.5M rows, too close to the archive job's memory ceiling) elapsed
# since the last successful upload. Self-gating means we can run this on a
# daily cron without forcing an exact-interval cron expression.
0 2 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli archive_if_due

# Receipt retention: purge discount-report receipt images older than 18
# months (privacy policy). Idempotent; the report row outlives the image.
30 3 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli cleanup_receipts

# Routing graph refresh. denver-map-prep rebuilds and re-uploads the .pbf at
# 02:00 Denver daily; this picks it up afterwards, once map-prep's ~50-minute
# window has closed. Downloads only when the R2 ETag changed, so most days it
# is a no-op. A changed .pbf is logged loudly: the valhalla container has to be
# recreated to rebuild tiles, and this container deliberately has no Docker
# socket to do that itself.
30 4 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli refresh_routing_graph

# Battery model. Reads the last ~26h of raw_telemetry_points, so it MUST run
# BEFORE the 02:00 archive, which flushes that table to R2 and truncates it.
# Running after would see only the handful of cycles since the truncate. 01:30
# leaves the full day in place; the 26h lookback overlaps the previous
# truncation boundary so nothing falls between two runs.
# Yields ~120 observations/day; the model becomes trainable after ~2 weeks.
# To seed it from history instead, see `backfill_battery_trips` (manual, needs
# a raised memory limit).
30 1 * * * cd /app && python -m src.cli extract_battery_trips

# Refit weekly. Runs after extraction has had its turn, and the coefficients
# move slowly enough that a daily refit would mostly chase weather noise.
45 5 * * 1 cd /app && python -m src.cli train_battery_model
